<Ui xmlns="http://www.blizzard.com/wow/ui/">

    <!--
        [G27] A description row for the settings list, defined here because no
        Blizzard element draws one. G23, G25 and G26 settled that between them:
        of every template this client has, only the section header draws
        arbitrary text as a heading, and only SettingsLanguageRestartNeeded
        draws it otherwise, as a control's label, ellipsised.

        Settings.CreateElementInitializer takes ANY template name, not just
        Blizzard's, so the question this answers is whether a template an AddOn
        ships itself will render in Blizzard's own settings list.

        Deliberately primitive. Nothing here relies on a mixin attribute, a
        Blizzard mixin table, or any inheritance: a plain Frame, a FontString,
        and an OnLoad that hangs one method on the frame by hand. If the modern
        XML features are present they are simply unused; if they are not, this
        still works. The point is to find out whether the template renders at
        all, not to write elegant XML.

        The FontString has a fixed width and no height, which is what makes it
        wrap instead of ellipsising. The ellipsis is the failure mode that
        ruled SettingsLanguageRestartNeededTemplate out.
    -->
    <Frame name="UnmarkedReconDescriptionTemplate" virtual="true">
        <Size x="600" y="40"/>
        <Layers>
            <Layer level="ARTWORK">
                <FontString parentKey="Text" inherits="GameFontHighlightSmall"
                            justifyH="LEFT" justifyV="TOP">
                    <Size x="560" y="0"/>
                    <Anchors>
                        <Anchor point="TOPLEFT" x="37" y="-4"/>
                    </Anchors>
                </FontString>
            </Layer>
        </Layers>
        <Scripts>
            <OnLoad function="UnmarkedRecon_DescriptionOnLoad"/>
        </Scripts>
    </Frame>

</Ui>
